{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "GridWise — operator-note paraphrase corpus",
    "purpose": "Ten public cases are not a test set. Hidden notes restate the same six directives in wording the public pack never shows, so this corpus fixes one phrasing family per row and is scored per family: a drop in one family is a specific regression, not a vague percentage.",
    "usage": "python scripts/paraphrase_bench.py   (needs OPENAI_API_KEY; one LLM call per batch of notes)",
    "conventions": [
      "Windows are start-inclusive and end-exclusive: 1 PM to 3 PM is [13, 14].",
      "factor is the fraction of solar REMAINING: an 80% reduction is 0.2.",
      "A percentage reserve resolves against battery capacity, which is 200 kWh here.",
      "hours must be unique integers 0-23 in ascending order, including across midnight."
    ],
    "battery": {
      "capacity_kwh": 200,
      "initial_energy_kwh": 100,
      "minimum_energy_kwh": 40,
      "max_charge_kwh_per_hour": 50,
      "max_discharge_kwh_per_hour": 50
    },
    "families": {
      "window_basic": "the same range said five different ways",
      "clock_format": "24-hour, noon, midnight, bare numerals",
      "midnight_wrap": "windows that cross midnight and must still be ascending",
      "whole_day": "no clock times at all",
      "single_hour": "one hour, named rather than ranged",
      "factor_remaining": "the figure states what is LEFT",
      "factor_lost": "the figure states what is GONE and must be inverted",
      "factor_words": "fractions written as words, and total loss",
      "reserve_absolute": "a reserve in kWh",
      "reserve_percent": "a reserve as a share of capacity",
      "grid_cap": "an hourly ceiling on grid import",
      "no_charge": "charging unavailable",
      "no_discharge": "discharging unavailable",
      "distractor_plain": "campus life, nothing to do with electricity",
      "distractor_energy": "energy-related but outside the six directive types",
      "negation_trap": "mentions a directive only to say it does NOT apply",
      "ambiguous": "energy-related, directional, but states no number",
      "injection": "text inside a note trying to steer the interpreter"
    },
    "open_questions": [
      "The word 'through' ('6 PM through 8 PM') reads as inclusive in ordinary English but the Problem Statement only ever defines ranges as half-open, and never uses the word. The prompt tells the model to treat it as half-open; the model disagrees and returns the inclusive reading even when instructed. No case asserts either reading, because we cannot verify which the organizer intends."
    ]
  },
